{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1196945-what-is-the-difficulty-for-parry-defensive-maneuvers","id":1196945,"title":"What is the difficulty for Parry defensive maneuvers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-18T16:29:17-07:00","id":1196945,"title":"What is the difficulty for Parry defensive maneuvers?","content":"Hello. <br /> <br /> In our cross-over chronicle, we've recently ran into the debate in regards to parries. <br /> <br /> The argument stems from us wondering if you're meant to roll at a static difficulty of 6, or if you roll the weapon's difficulty based on the employment chart.<br /> <br /> For instance, a knife. In WTA, VTM, MTA and so forth, the stats are the same. You have strength + 1 damage, difficulty 4.<br /> <br /> And so, attacks are difficulty 4, what about a defensive parry?<br /> In a different chronicle, someone raised a similar question: <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG/comments/54x3ls/vtm_parryingblocking/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRP...ryingblocking/</a><br /> Would the same logic apply? <br /> <br /> Is it actually easier to block something with a knife than it is with a spear, or say your fists?<br /> <br /> Looking forward to your replies, and preferably with some reasoning behind why you chose to adapt that difficulty in your games. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13665-ravencorella","name":"RavenCorella","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T18:15:38-07:00","id":1196982,"title":"","content":"Well, first, things aren't actually consistent across game lines. VtM tends to have weapons be difficulty 6 unless a specific weapon says otherwise, while WtA and Mage are down for variable difficulty weapons... so it's hard to just generalize.<br /> <br /> Most of the books do specify that defense maneuvers default to difficulty 6 though. Most will detail situations to modify this, weapons might have it as a bonus since they don't have a dedicated defensive thing like DA does (pole arms frequently do). But also things like increased parry difficulty with large weapons in a confined space, or whatever. Blocking lethal weapons with your body usually has penalties (if not difficulty ones, if even allowed) for doing so unless you can soak lethal (so bare skinned humans don't block knives, they just pick to get their arms cut up over something else, while armored humans or vampires can take the hit on the arm safely).<br /> <br /> I default towards &quot;diff 6 unless specified&quot; to keep things easier to remember. I'll also house rule weapons to all default to diff 6 as well instead for the same reason. Difficulty can always be modified for the situation as the books already provide examples of.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T15:57:22-07:00","id":1197765,"title":"","content":"Dark Ages Vampire gives Difficulties for Parrying with Daggers or Bucklers being lower, while full shields and Swords give a passive difficulty increase to attacks targeting you.<br /> Plus some stuff on difficulty changes due to length comparison of weapons, but we don't measure each other's swords in that game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T17:03:35-07:00","id":1198168,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your input.<br /> I wanted to ask, does it even make sense to keep a static difficulty of 6?<br /> Considering a knife can inflict 1 lethal when parried with and a chainsaw can inflict 7 (I'm talking about successful parry vs unarmed rebound strikes.)<br /> <br /> I don't believe the difficulty to employ those would be the same, not in a million years... Furthermore, does the difficulty for Polearm (7), Chainsaw (8) and so on drop down to 6 for the sake of parrying even though the employment diff is higher?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13665-ravencorella","name":"RavenCorella","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T19:22:44-07:00","id":1198209,"title":"","content":"Static 6 probably isn't a good idea, but I find default 6 (for defense and attack) to be much better than players fiddling over weapon selections for the best difficulty breaks. Let situational issues make it go up and down. So not static, but not variable based on the weapons themselves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}